invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
reason: rsa_sign64.c's use_ifma reads the multiply bit alone, so every
  session that states its multiply signs on AVX-512 IFMA and dies of
  SIGILL on a CPU without the instructions, whatever its caller probed.
  Every byte stays right on a CPU with them. bin/rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
  counts the kernel's calls and requires none from rsa_sign64_sp1 under a
  value without CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY;
    return (cpu & both) == both;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY) != 0;
